  "id": "goblet-squat-to-press",
  "name": "Goblet Squat to Press",
  "definition": "A bilateral controlled repetition combining one single-dumbbell goblet squat and a two-hand overhead press of the same dumbbell. The dumbbell begins vertical at the chest with both hands cupping its top head, the athlete squats to approximately thigh parallel or deeper as mobility allows, stands, then presses overhead without a second knee dip. Cavaggioni et al. name the single-dumbbell combined exercise in a training protocol, and NASM supports the chest-held goblet setup; neither source measured the complete transition, grip during overhead travel, muscle contribution, or a universal depth. The two-hand hold, ordered return, and categorical roles are bounded catalog choices and anatomy-and-mechanics inferences. A kettlebell, two-dumbbell shoulder rack, single-arm press, uninterrupted power thruster, or separate exercises are outside this family. Log the complete mass of one dumbbell once.",
